flowchart TD
    A([Hypothetical local pointwise Type I singularity at z_*])
    B{Terminal entry criterion}
    C[Admissible Type I package<br/>Type I bound + velocity concentration + terminal no-escape]
    D[Paper I Seregin extraction<br/>nonzero bounded ancient mild/Seregin profile U<br/>with retained compact local L3 concentration]

    A --> B
    B -->|local terminal no-escape theorem| C
    C --> D

    E{Paper I--III non-residual tests}
    D --> E

    L1[[Leaf: small-amplitude Type I singularity<br/>excluded by epsilon-regularity / Paper I]]
    L2[[Leaf: stationary L3 ancient singularity<br/>excluded by Paper I]]
    L3[[Leaf: uniformly L3-tight ancient singularity<br/>excluded by Paper II + endpoint Liouville]]
    L4[[Leaf: closed structured/decay singularity<br/>excluded by Paper III]]
    R[Coarse residual class R(S;I,J)<br/>all earlier alternatives removed]

    E -->|small amplitude?| L1
    E -->|stationary L3?| L2
    E -->|uniformly L3-tight?| L3
    E -->|closed structured/decay?| L4
    E -->|none of the above| R

    F{Refined residual ledger<br/>ordered branch criterion}
    R --> F

    R1[[Leaf: C_ax singularity<br/>axisymmetric bounded-circulation residual<br/>excluded by R1 axis-circulation Liouville]]
    R2[[Leaf: C_rot singularity<br/>rotational relative equilibrium<br/>excluded by localized Coriolis-flux rigidity]]
    R3[[Leaf: C_stat singularity<br/>degenerate stationary hull with retained concentration<br/>excluded by terminal concentration theorem]]
    R4[[Leaf: C_aff singularity<br/>affine/parasitic lower branch<br/>excluded by oscillatory-entry normalization]]

    F -->|axisymmetric bounded circulation?| R1
    F -->|rotational relative equilibrium?| R2
    F -->|stationary hull with retained concentration?| R3
    F -->|affine/parasitic lower branch?| R4

    T{Critical-tail criterion}
    F -->|critical-tail boundary defect?| T

    T1[[Leaf: C_logdiff singularity<br/>log-diffuse critical tail<br/>excluded by log-window descendants + hidden-scale closure]]
    T2[[Leaf: C_young singularity<br/>Young critical tail<br/>excluded by first-bad mesoscopic routing]]
    T3[[Leaf: C_homcrit singularity<br/>coherent homogeneous critical tail<br/>excluded by bounded-origin realization]]
    T4[[Leaf: C_logper singularity<br/>coherent log-periodic critical tail<br/>excluded by bounded-origin realization]]
    T5[[Leaf: C_apcrit singularity<br/>coherent aperiodic critical tail<br/>excluded by bounded-origin realization]]

    T -->|log-diffuse?| T1
    T -->|Young-measure tail?| T2
    T -->|homogeneous coherent tail?| T3
    T -->|log-periodic coherent tail?| T4
    T -->|aperiodic coherent tail?| T5

    G[C_gen generic terminal residual<br/>no named symmetry, no lower branch, no critical-tail stratum]
    F -->|none of the residual ledger branches above| G

    H{Terminal active-profile criterion}
    G --> H

    G1[[Leaf: mixed residual singularity<br/>compact retained core + diffuse or noncompact remainder<br/>excluded by no mixed compact--diffuse residual state]]
    G2[[Leaf: multi-profile singularity<br/>finite separated retained concentration profiles<br/>excluded by no finite separated-family theorem]]
    G3[[Leaf: active-descendant singularity<br/>finite loop or infinite active branch<br/>excluded by compact active path-space recurrence]]
    I[Single terminally indecomposable retained profile]

    H -->|mixed compact--diffuse/noncompact state?| G1
    H -->|two or more separated retained profiles?| G2
    H -->|active descendant branch or loop?| G3
    H -->|single profile; no tail limit, no diffuse tail, no noncompact recentering| I

    J{Endpoint criterion}
    I --> J

    G4[[Leaf: indecomposable L3-sequence singularity<br/>backward sequence tau_k to -infinity with bounded L3<br/>excluded by parasitic-free mildness + Albritton--Barker endpoint Liouville]]
    G5[[Leaf: failed sequence-L3 alternative<br/>forces diffuse/tail concentration or retained tail limit<br/>therefore returns to mixed, critical-tail, or active branch above]]

    J -->|sequence-L3 completeness holds| G4
    J -->|otherwise| G5

    Z([All leaves are impossible<br/>therefore no Type I singularity remains])
    L1 --> Z
    L2 --> Z
    L3 --> Z
    L4 --> Z
    R1 --> Z
    R2 --> Z
    R3 --> Z
    R4 --> Z
    T1 --> Z
    T2 --> Z
    T3 --> Z
    T4 --> Z
    T5 --> Z
    G1 --> Z
    G2 --> Z
    G3 --> Z
    G4 --> Z
    G5 --> Z

